Z||000001||pHoOl||12-09-2001||01:25 AM||||Well, it has to do with the time.  He passes through different time zones all the time.  not to mention the different conversion rates for time.  for instance.... 1 US hour equals approx 1.66 canadian hours.  (Just like currency) So... he has the shortest amount of time to spend in the US, cause our dollar is worth more than most other currency.  So you see, he really has 39.84 canadian hours to do it.  not to mention when you start getting into Yen.  <P><BR>But actually... i remember seeing somethign about how somebody figured out exactly how fast he'd have to go, and the acceleration, and G forces.  Really wild... all i can say is someone proved their geekiness<P>Edited errors which confused meaning<BR>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>          <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by pHoOl (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
